  1.000000: kin_tf

  
 =====================================================================================================
 Frozen Density Embedding to include enviroment effects using the fixed potential method described in:
 A.S.P. Gomes, C. R. Jacob and L. Visscher, Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys. 10 (2008) 5353–5362.
 =====================================================================================================

  Frozen Density Embedding Calculation set-up:
  --------------------------------------------

 * Print level:     0
 * FDE Potential read from file: EMBPOT                                                      


   Kohn-Sham calculation set-up
   ----------------------------

 * Print level:     2
 * Numerical integration grid:
   - integration grid imported from file EMBGRD                        
 * DFT thresholds:
   - dfthr0 =  0.10000E-08
   - dfthri =  0.20000E-11
 * Spin density contribution in response calculations:
   - use the norm of the spin magnetization vector as a definition of the spin density (noncollinear definition)
 * Adiabatic local density approximation (ALDA):
   - approximate all functional derivatives beyond the xc potential by SVWN derivatives
   - for hybrid functionals exact exchange is switched off in the solution of the response equation
     (if you want to keep it, use .XALDA)


